the surface can't express -> a compliant reason-required bug close is UNREACHABLE'","Plan prose specifies rewriting force/audit prose but is silent on documenting the reason-required class vocabulary or the non-force+class conditional"],"finding":"The plan requires exposing a new `reason` parameter on transition_ticket and rewriting the LLM-facing tool prose to the absent-attestation audit model, but does not require that prose to co-locate the decision rule governing WHEN reason is required/persisted. Per _lib_writes.py, `reason` persists as close_reason ONLY on a non-force close whose close_class is in REASON_REQUIRED_CLASSES {obsolete, wontfix, not_a_bug, escalated}; otherwise it is the force audit comment. Without this rule stated in the tool docstring the model reads, an agent cannot know when a reason-required close needs reason — the very 'A->C trap' the ticket's experiment (comment 3) identified.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe7ddb70523a3bc67","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Repair plan bullet 'Replace the rescinded no-force tool prose...' and AC line 'MCP tool prose describes absent certification as the audit signal'","norm_id":"n238e75be307d8695","priority":0.268,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An MCP agent attempts a reason-required close (e.g. not_a_bug/wontfix) and omits reason because the docstring never says reason is required for those classes","An agent supplies reason on a force close or a non-reason-required class and is surprised it is silently discarded"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add to the Repair plan / AC that the transition_ticket docstring must name the reason-required close_class vocabulary and state that `reason` is persisted as close_reason only on a non-force close whose class is in that set, and otherwise serves as the force audit comment.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cit